Commentary of al-Shinqiti (Adwa' al-Bayan) on surah 15, verse 81:

The words of the Exalted: ﴿And We gave them Our signs, but they turned away from them.﴾

In this noble verse, the Exalted mentions that He gave the companions of al-Hijr, who are Thamud, His signs, but they turned away from them. Al-i'rad (turning away) is to shun something and not pay heed to it. It seems to be derived from al-'arad (العُرْض), with a damma, meaning the side; for the one who turns away does not turn his face, but rather bends his side, turning aside and repelling.

Here the Majestic and Exalted does not specify any of those signs which He gave them, nor the manner of their turning away from them, but He has explained that in other places. He explained that among the greatest of the signs given to them was that she-camel which Allah brought forth for them. Indeed, some scholars have said that in the aforementioned she-camel there were many signs: her emerging pregnant (ushara'), with a red-brown coat (bara'), hollow-bodied (jawfa'), out of a solid, hard rock; the swiftness of her giving birth upon emerging; her great size, such that no camel resembled her; the abundance of her milk, sufficient for all of them; and the abundance of her drinking, as the Exalted said: ﴿For her is a share of water, and for you is a share on a known day﴾ [al-Shu'ara': 155], and He said: ﴿And inform them that the water is divided between them, each share attended﴾ [al-Qamar: 28].

Knowing this, be aware that among what clarifies the words of the Exalted, ﴿And We gave them Our signs﴾ [al-Hijr: 81], is His saying: ﴿Then bring a sign, if you are of the truthful.﴾ He said: ﴿This is a she-camel; for her is a share of water, and for you is a share on a known day﴾ [al-Shu'ara': 154-155]; and His saying: ﴿There has certainly come to you clear evidence from your Lord. This is the she-camel of Allah, a sign for you, so leave her to eat in the earth of Allah and do not touch her with harm﴾ [al-A'raf: 73], to the end of the verse; and His saying: ﴿And We gave Thamud the she-camel as a visible sign﴾ [al-Isra': 59]; and His saying: ﴿Indeed, We are sending the she-camel as a trial for them, so watch them and be patient﴾ [al-Qamar: 27]; and His saying: ﴿And O my people, this is the she-camel of Allah, a sign for you, so leave her to eat in the earth of Allah and do not touch her with harm, lest you be seized by a near punishment﴾ [Hud: 64]; and other signs besides these.

And He explained the turning away of the people of Salih from those signs in many places:

• As in His saying: ﴿And they hamstrung the she-camel and defied the command of their Lord and said, "O Salih, bring us what you have threatened us with, if you are of the messengers"﴾ [al-A'raf: 77];

• And His saying: ﴿So they hamstrung her, and he said, "Enjoy yourselves in your homes for three days"﴾ ... to the end of the verse [Hud: 65];

• And His saying: ﴿Thamud denied in their transgression, when the most wretched of them was sent forth. And the messenger of Allah said to them, "The she-camel of Allah and her drink!" But they denied him and hamstrung her, so their Lord destroyed them for their sin and leveled them﴾ ... [al-Shams: 11-14];

• And His saying: ﴿But they called their companion, and he took [her] and hamstrung her﴾ [al-Qamar: 29].

• And His saying: ﴿And We gave Thamud the she-camel as a visible sign, but they wronged themselves through her﴾ [al-Isra': 59];

• And His saying: ﴿They said, "You are only of those affected by magic. You are not but a human like us"﴾ ... to the end of the verse [al-Shu'ara': 185-186].

And other signs besides these.
